      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    long long n, p, t;\n\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &n);\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &p);\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &t);\n\n    if (n == 1) {\n        printf(\"0\\n\");\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    long long period = 2 * (n - 1);\n    long long pos = (p + t) % period;\n\n    if (pos >= n)\n        pos = period - pos;\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", pos);\n}",
      "statement": "A token moves inside a hallway containing positions {{0}} to [[n]]-{{1}}.\n\nIt starts at position [[p]] and initially moves toward larger positions.\n\nAt each step, the token moves exactly {{1}} position.\n\nIf the next move would cause the token to leave the hallway, it first reverses direction, then moves.\n\nOutput the position of the token after [[t]] steps.",
